","The relationship used to estimate the floggability limits of mixtures from the data for individual freements is the **Law of Limits**, which states that the flattability limits of a mixture are the **average** of the flattability limits of the individual freets. This law can be used to estimate the flattability limits of a mixture by the following formulas:
\[
\text{Upper Limit}_{\text{mixture}} = \frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n} \left(\text{Upper Limit}_{i} \times \text{Concentability}_{i}\right)}{\sum_{i=1}^{n} \text{Concentabilitability}_{i}}
\]
\[
\text{Lower Limit}_{\text{mixture}} = \frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n} \left(\text{Lower Limit}_{i} \times \text{Concentabilitty}_{i}\right)}{\sum_{i=1}^{n} \text{Concentabilitably}_{i}}
\]
Here, the lower and upper limits of the mixture are calculated by the weighted average of the lower and upper limits of the individual freets, respectively, where the weights are the concentrations of the freets.",relevance,"# Task Description
