The coordination geometry of the iron (i3) in ethyl (3) tetraperorphalx is complex and not straightforward, but the most mostption is a **triangular-trihedral (or triangular-trihedral)** shape. This means the iron atom has three sides, each being a triangle, with the three corners of each triangle corresponding to the three vertices of the triangle.
