\int_{0}^{1}\left(3 e^{x}+2 \sqrt{x}\right) d x = 3 \int_{0}^{1} e^{x} d x + 2 \int_{0}^{1} \sqrt{x} d x = 3 \left[ e^{x} \right]_{0}^{1} + 2 \left[ \frac{2}{3} x^{3/2} \right]_{0}^{1} = 3 (e^{1} - e^{0}) + 2 \left( \frac{2}{3} (1)^{3/2} - 0 \right) = 3 (e - 1) + \frac{4}{3} = 3e - 3 + \frac{4}{3} = 3e - \frac{5}{3}.
\]
