\[
\mathbf{r}(t) = \mathbf{r}_0 + t \mathbf{n},
\]

where \(\mathbf{r}_0\) is the position vector of the point \((4,2,-2)\), and \(\mathbf{n}\) is the normal vector. Thus,

\[
\mathbf{r}(t) = (4, 2, -2) + t(8, 4, -36).
\]

