2. **Time-in-state normalization**: The probability of finding the system in the state \(\psi_n\) at time \(t\) is given by the inner product \(\langle \psi_n | \psi_t \rangle\), where \(\psi_t\) is the wave function at time \(t\). The unitarity condition implies that the probability of finding the system in any state is 1, so the wave functions must be normalized such that the probability of finding the system in any state is 1.

