   - The unitarity condition states that \(\sum_l S_{lm}^* S_{ln} = \delta_{mn}\).
   - The left-hand side of the equation is the inner product of the \(S\)-matrix with its conjugate:
     \[
     \sum_l S_{lm}^* S_{ln} = \langle \psi_m | S^* S \psi_n \rangle
     \]
   - The unitarity condition implies that the \(S\)-matrix is unitary, i.e., \(S^* S = I\), where \(I\) is the identity matrix. Thus, the right-hand side of the equation is:
